WEBVTT

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:33.770
I received a directive from CEO Kiyonami to suspend the research.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.360
Telling me to stop now would be just like letting him die.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.690
On the 13th we escaped with our findings.

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:48.720
I'm going to monitor the research subject for a period of time.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.420
We killed a man in order to procure the necessary funds.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:54.800
There's no turning back now.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:58.760
His condition is improving.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:03.070
His metabolism has increased and I've begun administering him medicine for the fever.

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:10.450
No additional side-effects spotted so far.

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:32.920
Do you hate me?

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.920
Enough to want to kill me?

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.370
You're a researcher yourself.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:53.860
Right from the beginning, you must have predicted this possibility.

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:58.320
It's all terrible...

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.650
My... heart...

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:03.580
My body...

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.370
Let's continue with the medication.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.540
I want the materials I had during the great war.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:13.240
There's only one person who can help complete my research.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:15.470
Twenty Faces left behind the information I need.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:20.200
He must have included what we need in his legacy.

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:23.360
Mikamo Chizuko.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.210
The daughter of Twenty Faces.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:27.810
She's the key.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.910
Young lady, you have a visitor here to see you.

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:52.000
Uncle Genji!

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:57.310
Chiko!  I barely recognize you, Chiko.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:59.960
Would it be impolite for me to hug you like in the old days?

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:02.610
Oh my.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:13.820
I meant to come earlier, but ever since Shiyanouji—no, your parents passed away,

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.840
I've felt very awkward about coming to this house.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:19.550
And, truth be told, I can't stand that gaudy aunt of yours.

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:22.780
Was it difficult for you?

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.780
Nope.  Not at all.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:29.710
Oh.  Speaking of which, it's not just that you grew up.

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:31.270
There's something else...

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.900
I guess two years is a long time.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:39.450
It passed in the blink of an eye.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:40.730
Is that so?

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:41.670
Yes.

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:45.680
I'm truly grateful to Detective Akine.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.380
He's got a good head on his shoulders.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:53.060
Maybe I should be asking him.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:56.810
The thing is, there's someone I want him to find for me.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:59.080
You shouldn't do that, Akine-sensei!

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:01.940
You're the one who shouldn't!  Letting her see visitors in secret.

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:04.670
I'm sorry for interrupting your conversation–

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.590
Why, hello.  My name is Detective Akine.

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:11.700
I'm the one who has been entrusted to handle Chizuko-san's affairs.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.980
Oh, I'm well aware.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:19.720
We were actually just discussing the fact that I'd like your assistance with something.

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:22.720
Oh, do tell, do tell.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:31.100
Ah.  Ah-Ah-Ah.  Aren't you going a little fast?

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.530
Have no worries, Detective.

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:37.260
However, I wasn't really planning on having Chiko meet him.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:40.720
I'm old enough to know when to be quiet when adults are talking.

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:41.860
I see.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:47.180
I can't get near Twenty Faces while I'm cooped up in that house.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:50.870
I've just got to watch, listen and think for myself.

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:54.390
Sign:  Kiyonami Pharmaceuticals

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:57.480
Let me introduce you, CEO Kiyonami.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:59.860
This is Detective Akine.

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:02.300
We appreciate all your efforts.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:04.440
Never fear when I'm on the case!

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:06.910
And this young lady?

00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:08.700
This is Mikamo Chizuko.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:11.430
Under the circumstances, we had to bring her with us.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.140
Are you Mr. Mikamo's daughter?

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:17.640
I knew your father quite well while he was still alive.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.140
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:22.900
I know that you're a busy man, sir.  Let's get to the main issues.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:26.900
The thing is, I'd like you to locate these people.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:31.370
Kayama Nozomi and Tsuya Takashi.  They're two of my researchers.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:37.290
They disappeared three months ago along with all their research data and materials.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.380
Maybe they eloped?

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:41.040
I'm jealous!

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:46.550
Their research was for a weapon for the war.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:49.260
It was a top-secret project.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.550
My, my.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:55.560
I'm not sure we'll get all the help we need from the police.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.300
This'll net me a pretty penny.

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:00.580
A weapon for the war.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:04.500
Didn't Twenty Faces and the rest mention that too?

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.820
Do you think you can do something for him, Akine-san?

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:17.310
I'm certain they'll expose their whereabouts to me.

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:18.830
It's only a matter of time.

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:22.370
That's reassuring.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:26.960
I don't want to cause Uncle Genji any trouble, though.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:30.030
I wonder what this weapon is anyway.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:31.840
Twenty Faces might have known about it.

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:48.130
Sign:  I've come back to get you. —Twenty Faces

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:54.640
Oh my, I wonder what's written there.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:57.010
Nothing.  It's just a piece of paper.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:58.780
Wanna see?

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:09.390
The writing's gone!

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:11.010
How'd she do that?

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:15.380
Th-That shouldn't be!  I wrote it just–

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.800
Where did you learn sleight of hand like that?

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:24.020
I wish the note had been real.

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:37.910
Miss, your name's Mikamo, right?

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:39.910
I was asked to give this to you.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:45.070
Who's it from?

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:49.760
That's definitely his mark.

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:54.580
But something like this could give him away to the police.

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:56.720
This can't really be from him.

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:05.670
Watch, listen, and think for myself.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:08.940
Trust in myself.  That's what he said.

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.840
Must be my imagination.

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:47.990
You're Mikamo Chizuko-san, right?

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:51.650
I'm a messenger from Twenty Faces.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:55.260
Did she say Twenty Faces?

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:56.860
This sounds like a great adventure.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:23.910
Sayuri-san, Mika-san?  What are you doing here?

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:25.730
That was incredible, Chiko-san.

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:27.660
I can't believe you jumped over that wall.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.100
Just... forget about that.  Why are you here?

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.150
Just... forget about that.  Why are you here?

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:35.920
Oh, right!  Koito-san is in trouble!

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:37.050
She caught a glimpse of it and...

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:42.940
I can't believe I'm going to Twenty Faces' hideout.

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:45.120
What a great adventure.

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:58.830
You're not Mikamo Chizuko.

00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:00.190
What's the meaning of this?

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:02.780
What a shame.  I've been found out already?

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:08.770
But if this is a kidnapping, I'm worth even more money than Mikamo-san.

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:11.940
Money has nothing to do with it.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:15.520
If you're just looking to stave off boredom, I can get you something expensive, young lady.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:19.720
I'd rather you let me have some fun than buying me something expensive.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:21.050
That's all I'm looking for.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:24.910
I haven't much time left.

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:31.040
I've got to have as much fun as possible before I turn 16 and have my arranged marriage.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.670
It is my life, after all.

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:43.400
"My Life as a Detective:  Twenty Faces and I."

00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:46.330
What a great title!

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:47.450
This'll sell for sure.

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:50.610
What should I do about the actual contents?

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:52.940
Well, I'll just let the papers figure that out.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:54.350
Akine-san!

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:55.310
Chizuko-kun!

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:57.320
There's been a kidnapping!

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.820
Wha-wha-wha?!

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:01.870
Wow!

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:03.260
An adventure!

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:06.070
It's late.  You two should go home.

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:07.610
No way!

00:12:07.610 --> 00:12:10.860
I mean, we're eyewitnesses after all!

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:14.910
Well, with me accompanying you, you have nothing to worry about.

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:17.690
This is like something out of a detective novel!

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:19.210
My heart's pounding.

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:25.420
A patrol car?

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:28.560
The fun you've been waiting for is about to start.

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:32.060
You should speed up a little, Mr. Detective.

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:34.640
Yeah.  You'll never catch up to them at this rate.

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:38.750
It's a straight road with barely any cars on it.  We'll catch them in no time.

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:41.320
There.  We passed them.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.150
Those are their tire-tracks.

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:45.970
Why do you think they took that road?

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:51.700
Those are fresh tracks.  They must've turned into that narrow road at high speed.

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:56.230
I suppose it's worth checking out.

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:07.210
She's got a child with her.

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:07.660
Move in!

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:10.270
You should go.

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:13.380
Huh?  You're not going to take me hostage and escape?

00:13:13.380 --> 00:13:15.780
The kidnapping ends here.

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:17.900
I'm ending it myself.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:21.500
Apprehend her!

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:25.650
What incredible strength!

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:26.910
I'm not running.

00:13:29.710 --> 00:13:31.100
Kayama-kun.

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:34.100
I guess it was only a matter of time until you found me.

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:35.740
You robbed that bank.

00:13:35.740 --> 00:13:38.740
You needed the money to continue development, didn't you?

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:40.670
Is that how you tracked me down?

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:42.800
You were always so dedicated.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.050
You couldn't just leave it alone.

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:53.330
Ah-Ah, what's going on here?

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:58.310
Well well, that's the detective I know.  Good job finding the place.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:13:59.640
Oh, right.  Of course.

00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:02.020
Oh, right.  Of course.

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:06.070
Oh, whatever.

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:08.050
Koito-san.

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:10.230
Chiko-san, that's the woman.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:13.470
That's the one who picked up Koito-san.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:15.950
Mikamo Chizuko.

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:19.460
Why did she use Twenty Faces' name to try and get to me?

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:25.590
The daughter of Twenty Faces...

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:29.670
Kayama-kun, when did you decide to go to such extremes?

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:34.350
We're running out of time.  He's on the verge of death.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:37.020
The research from the war.

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:40.020
Twenty Faces' legacy.

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:55.830
Is that Tsuya-kun?

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:58.390
The fruits of our efforts.

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:00.100
Or rather, the abomination we created.

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:13.510
Run!

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.030
Hurry!

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:21.810
Amazing.

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:22.790
What are you doing?!

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:37.600
Tsuya!

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:39.100
His mind is warped.

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:40.570
Stop!  You'll kill them!

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:44.510
The daughter of Twenty Faces!

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:46.090
Twenty Faces' legacy!

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:50.210
He's after me.

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:06.770
It's OK, Sayuri-san, Mika-san.

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:08.860
H-Help us.

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:10.280
I hate this!

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:18.600
The daughter of Twenty Faces!

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:21.290
Twenty Faces' legacy!

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:24.290
I need to draw him away from everyone.

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:40.850
Someone grab that girl!

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:42.400
Yes, sir!

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:43.600
Tsuya-kun...

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.540
It was necessary.

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:50.760
For Twenty Faces' legacy.  The top-secret research data from the war.

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:52.860
We were going to continue that research.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:56.610
What?  Research?

00:16:56.610 --> 00:17:01.930
The materials from the end of the war.  The data this country produced.

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:08.130
It would have been the ultimate weapon.  It was for the good of mankind.

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:11.630
It's despicable to imagine you'd continue that research.

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:18.010
Even so, as a researcher, I had to know what we were on the verge of creating.

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:23.550
A plan for a weapon designed to unlock the true potential of humanity.

00:17:23.550 --> 00:17:27.970
We can use it to rewrite the path that humanity is on.

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:29.340
This is revolutionary research.

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:36.490
All the research done on animals was perfect.
We just needed a human test subject.

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:40.470
However, we never got to experiment on a human.

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:41.990
And our country lost the war.

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:47.050
I believe that we were on the verge of something great.

00:17:48.890 --> 00:17:51.630
So did he and so did Twenty Faces.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:57.690
But there's no proof.  Even the police investigation turned up nothing.

00:17:57.690 --> 00:18:01.760
The research never yielded anything.  It's all over.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:04.290
No.  It's not over.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:08.020
Is Tsuya-kun after Mikamo Chizuko-kun?

00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:12.270
Yes.  The one known as the daughter of Twenty Faces.

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:14.530
She's our only hope.

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:17.490
I should have stopped you earlier.

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:19.990
Before this horrible turn of events.

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:24.950
No one can stop him now.

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:44.560
I beg you.  Tell me!

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:47.430
Tell me the location of Twenty Faces' legacy!

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:49.180
No.

00:18:49.180 --> 00:18:50.870
I need to jump with all my power.

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:05.580
I don't want to hurt you.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:07.370
But I've lost control of my body!

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:43.600
It's over, Tsuya.

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:47.660
We lost to the geniuses of the war.

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:50.310
You too, Kayama-kun?

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:54.140
I'm a researcher as well.

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:59.420
Oh, Mikamo Chizuko-san.

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:03.160
I'm so sorry.  I just wanted to ask you a question.

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:07.140
How I could turn this body back to normal.

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:13.640
I'm sorry.  All I got from him were memories.

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:15.300
I see.

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:17.290
Then...

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:19.650
Maybe someday...

00:20:27.070 --> 00:20:27.680
Excuse me.

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:30.200
You're well-known.

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:32.540
There are people after you.

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:33.750
Be careful.

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:38.890
Hey...

00:20:38.890 --> 00:20:39.940
What a woman.

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:43.610
What is it?  "Twenty Faces' legacy"?

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:49.300
Ow!  It hurts!

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:52.110
Look, it's bleeding.  It's bleeding!

00:20:52.110 --> 00:20:53.430
We know.

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:55.100
Sayuri-san.  Mika-san.

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:59.630
Are you all right?  Did you get hurt?

00:20:59.630 --> 00:21:02.070
W-We're fine, Mikamo-san.

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:04.400
Well, we should be leaving now.

00:21:13.380 --> 00:21:16.120
It looks like it'll never be boring with you around.

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:18.130
Don't you agree, Chiko?

00:22:46.660 --> 00:22:51.430
This broadcast has been brought to you by these sponsors.
